        <mxCell id="d-notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*1 What was measured, and what was composed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each output's default configuration was counted from an actual&lt;br&gt;deployment. The data path below the access point is this portal's&lt;br&gt;real configuration. The figure joins the two; the portal itself&lt;br&gt;has only ever run on Amplify Gen 2&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*2 How the scope was matched&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;All three figures are matched to one scope: web, auth, API and a&lt;br&gt;table. This portal's implementation is larger than that; its AI&lt;br&gt;processing and audit paths are in the Part 1 figures&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;*3 No official icon exists&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;AWS Blocks and Nx Plugin for AWS have no official architecture&lt;br&gt;icon as of 2026-09. Both run at generation time rather than at&lt;br&gt;runtime, so these figures draw only the AWS resources they&lt;br&gt;generate" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=8 4;strokeColor=#E6EDF3;fillColor=#21262D;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=17;fontColor=#E6EDF3;" vertex="1" parent="1">
